      "title": "Tell HN: OpenAI brings back 5 hour limit for plus and business standard users",
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49600233",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49600233",
      "score": 127,
      "comments": 143,
      "author": "spwa4",
      "published": "2026-09-07T16:40:32Z",
      "bullets": [
        "OpenAI reinstated a 5-hour rate limit reset window for ChatGPT Plus and Business Standard tiers, replacing shorter reset intervals.",
        "The extended duration effectively decreases overall prompt throughput and diminishes the value of frequent quota refreshes for power users.",
        "Engineering workflows heavily dependent on interactive web sessions for models like GPT-4o face increased throttling pressure versus direct API usage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "x86 evolution for segmentation and paging",
      "url": "https://inbox.sourceware.org/binutils/CAKSQd8XJVf3jq8boOJcOE_GzcNvcqMUHeW-whbw3uGnVE2iN_w@mail.gmail.com/",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/1baq3m",
      "score": 6,
      "comments": 3,
      "author": "goliath",
      "published": "2026-09-08T10:22:13Z",
      "bullets": [
        "x86 shifted from 16-bit real-mode segment bases to 32-bit protected-mode descriptors, eventually deprecating hardware segmentation in x86-64 long mode.",
        "Paging matured from 80386 two-level 4KB schemes into 36-bit PAE and 48-bit four-level page tables (PML4) for 64-bit virtual memory.",
        "Modern extensions add 5-level paging (PML5) for 57-bit addressing, standardizing 2MB/1GB huge pages while relying purely on paging for memory isolation."
      ]
    },
